WEBVTT

q0001
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.808
If rows can be computed independently, why not always send every row to another worker?

q0002
00:00:07.808 --> 00:00:16.994
This episode has one job: Parallel CM partitions eligible materialization work into deterministic chunks, then reassembles the same exact output while charging scheduling and data-movement overhead.

q0003
00:00:16.994 --> 00:00:26.180
We build on Hybrid versus partial-hybrid materialization; their definitions stay fixed while this lesson adds a new layer.

q0004
00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:33.498
Parallel materialization divides eligible output work into chunks and deterministically reconstructs the same result.

q0005
00:00:33.498 --> 00:00:41.306
Watch for the label parallel materialization; it stays attached to the artifact this episode means.

q0006
00:00:41.306 --> 00:00:48.624
When we say work chunk, the highlight identifies its layer before we interpret it.

q0007
00:00:48.624 --> 00:00:57.412
The term shared memory receives its own visual state so it cannot drift into a neighboring concept.

q0008
00:00:57.412 --> 00:01:03.750
We will keep deterministic assembly visible whenever its definition controls the inference.

q0009
00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:12.538
The next sequence uses Four-variable truth layout as a conceptual teaching example, not as measured benchmark evidence.

q0010
00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:16.427
Our stable example is Four-variable truth layout.

q0011
00:01:16.427 --> 00:01:25.613
F(A,B,C,D)=(A AND B) XOR (C OR D), row variables A,B, column variables C,D, MSB-first ordering.

q0012
00:01:25.613 --> 00:01:32.931
Carry assignments, live support, explicit CM, packed truth vectors, and exact output across episodes.

q0013
00:01:32.931 --> 00:01:40.249
We now construct the Four-variable truth layout and name every part before interpreting it.

q0014
00:01:40.249 --> 00:01:48.547
Partition matrix rows into ordered chunks, send them through worker lanes, and keep global indices attached.

q0015
00:01:48.547 --> 00:01:56.355
Reassemble chunks in deterministic order while an overhead band shows scheduling, transfer, and merge work.

q0016
00:01:56.355 --> 00:02:01.224
Now isolate parallel work eligibility inside Four-variable truth layout.

q0017
00:02:01.224 --> 00:02:10.012
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for parallel work eligibility changes.

q0018
00:02:10.012 --> 00:02:18.800
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to parallel work eligibility, not to a substituted workload.

q0019
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:24.159
A matrix gains chunk boundaries only after minimum-work guards pass.

q0020
00:02:24.159 --> 00:02:29.028
Now isolate chunk/worker partition inside Four-variable truth layout.

q0021
00:02:29.028 --> 00:02:37.816
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for chunk/worker partition changes.

q0022
00:02:37.816 --> 00:02:46.604
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to chunk/worker partition, not to a substituted workload.

q0023
00:02:46.604 --> 00:02:51.963
Ordered tiles enter worker swim lanes with stable row-index tags.

q0024
00:02:51.963 --> 00:03:01.149
Parallel CM partitions eligible materialization work and deterministically assembles the result; parallel availability does not imply a speedup after scheduling and transport overhead.

q0025
00:03:01.149 --> 00:03:06.997
Read that statement only within this scope: current parallel CM implementation.

q0026
00:03:06.997 --> 00:03:10.886
Its declared measurement boundary is materialization strategy.

q0027
00:03:10.886 --> 00:03:15.265
The uncertainty field says no universal performance claim.

q0028
00:03:15.265 --> 00:03:24.451
The nearest confusing lesson is Pair-aware CM collapse; it owns pair eligibility, while this episode owns parallel work eligibility.

q0029
00:03:24.451 --> 00:03:33.637
The example fixes F of A, B, C, and D as A AND B, exclusive-or C OR D.

q0030
00:03:33.637 --> 00:03:39.485
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate parallel work eligibility.

q0031
00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:48.671
A and B select the row, C and D select the column, and MSB-first order fixes both index conventions.

q0032
00:03:48.671 --> 00:03:54.519
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate chunk/worker partition.

q0033
00:03:54.519 --> 00:04:02.327
Folding the truth-table output column into a four-by-four grid changes the layout, not the function.

q0034
00:04:02.327 --> 00:04:11.513
Reading a cell forward evaluates an assignment; reading it backward recovers the row and column bits that selected it.

q0035
00:04:11.513 --> 00:04:18.831
Parallelism adds scheduling and data-movement cost, so availability is not evidence of a speedup.

q0036
00:04:18.831 --> 00:04:26.149
Choose whether a small, large, or dependency-coupled case should cross the parallel work guard.

q0037
00:04:26.149 --> 00:04:32.977
Parallelism redistributes work; it does not remove the need to count the work.

q0038
00:04:32.977 --> 00:04:38.336
Now isolate deterministic assembly and overhead inside Four-variable truth layout.

q0039
00:04:38.336 --> 00:04:47.522
The example definition and output meaning stay fixed while only the state for deterministic assembly and overhead changes.

q0040
00:04:47.522 --> 00:04:56.708
That matched before-and-after view assigns the visible consequence to deterministic assembly and overhead, not to a substituted workload.

q0041
00:04:56.708 --> 00:05:03.536
Tiles return to one exact matrix while overhead remains a separate visible band.

q0042
00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:12.722
Every four-bit assignment names exactly one of the sixteen cells, and every cell returns one exact output bit.

q0043
00:05:12.722 --> 00:05:19.060
Holding that element fixed lets this episode isolate deterministic assembly and overhead.

q0044
00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:28.246
Live support can remove an input from active computation even when the ambient layout still reserves its axis.

q0045
00:05:28.246 --> 00:05:34.584
A common mistake is this: More workers necessarily make every materialization faster.

q0046
00:05:34.584 --> 00:05:40.432
Repair it by returning to the owned distinction: parallel work eligibility.

q0048
00:05:43.494 --> 00:05:52.680
Use the episode's central distinction to answer: Parallelism redistributes work; it does not remove the need to count the work.

q0049
00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:59.998
Parallel work is useful only after its independent work and overhead are both visible.
